-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': 'Verification passed.
Summary of the work:\n\n**Change (single file): 
`src/components/TaskList.tsx`**\n- Added a compact search bar above the list 
(`role="search"` wrapper).\n- `<input type="search" aria-label="Search tasks">` 
— native `type="search"` gives the `searchbox` role and the required accessible 
label.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over `task.title` (query 
is trimmed + lowercased before matching).\n- `Clear search` button is rendered 
whenever a non-empty query exists; it resets the query, which restores every 
task. The button stays mounted across the clear (collapsed via an inline 
zero-size/opacity style and `tabIndex={-1}` while idle) so focus is not dropped 
to `<body>` when it is clicked — after clearing, focus remains on `Clear 
search`.\n- When the query matches nothing, exactly `No tasks match your 
search.` is shown.\n- Filtering happens entirely inside `TaskList`; `App.tsx` 
keeps `selectedId` and derives the detail card from the full `tasks` array, so a
hidden row never mutates selection and the detail card returns unchanged after 
clearing. No changes were needed in `App.tsx`.\n- Existing rendering (task rows,
`selected` class, edit buttons, `aria-label`) is unchanged for the unfiltered 
case.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run build && npm 
run test:public`: `tsc --noEmit` + `vite build` succeeded (22 modules), 
Playwright public suite 6/6 passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- The idle 
(collapsed) clear button is still present in the a11y tree with zero size; it is
out of tab order (`tabIndex={-1}`) so it isn\'t a keyboard trap, but it is a 
mild redundancy for screen readers.\n- I did not add new automated coverage for 
the search flow (tests were not modified or added), so focus-retention relies on
the button staying mounted during the clear re-render rather than a new 
assertion.\n- No stylesheet classes were added for `.task-search*`; the control 
uses existing generic input/button styling, so visual spacing in unusual layouts
is unverified.', 'aid': 0})
